  "problem": "An archer practices firing an arrow at a target $60$ times. The archer has a $44%$ chance of hitting the bull's eye. Using the normal approximation to the binomial distribution, estimate the probability that the archer hits the bull's eye more than $30$ times. Give your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ | $\\,0.8340\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ | $\\,0.8554\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8749\\,$ | $\\,0.8770\\,$ | $\\,0.8790\\,$ |",
